[
    {
        "content": "<p>I vaguely remember reading about a new(ish) feature a while ago that allowed one to defer proof terms in a <code>def</code> until a special block at the end of the <code>def</code> that allows you to solve them all at once in tactic mode. The proof terms in the body of the <code>def</code> are replaced with named holes (e.g. <code>?foo</code>), and they become the names of goals in the special block at the end. Unfortunately I cannot for the life of me remember what the keyword is to enter this special block. It also seems to be ungoogleable. Any ideas?</p>",
        "id": 579060105,
        "sender_full_name": "Dylan Ede",
        "timestamp": 1773352117
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I remember this, but I think is was just a demo, not a deployed feature.</p>",
        "id": 579060834,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773352522
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You're talking about <code>where finally</code>; you're right though, this syntax seems to be documented nowhere. For reference:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">startPos</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">startPos_eq_endPos_iff</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList_eq_nil_iff</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 579061327,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1773352782
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you! I had started to doubt my memory (and sanity) when searching for this.</p>",
        "id": 579061682,
        "sender_full_name": "Dylan Ede",
        "timestamp": 1773352952
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Only documentation I can see is <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/find/?domain=Verso.Genre.Manual.section&amp;name=The-Lean-Language-Reference--Release-Notes--Lean-4___22___0-_LPAR_2025-08-14_RPAR_--Highlights--finally-section\">in the release notes for 4.22.0</a>.</p>",
        "id": 579063029,
        "sender_full_name": "Dylan Ede",
        "timestamp": 1773353675
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's a wondeful feature!</p>",
